{"context":"Workers must be organized to cover discussion, execution and review without coupling EKA to roles. EKA is removing ownership, so roles cannot live in the EKA store as assignments.","decision":"Worker roles (discuss, implement, review) are steward-controlled configuration binding role -\u003e ACP driver -\u003e prompt template. Roles never touch EKA, never decide control flow, and are not EKA knowledge artifacts. Reviewer roles are selected by code, independent of the author role where configured.","consequences":"Roles evolve with steward config, not the EKA store; EKA stays model-agnostic. Review independence is code-enforced. Cost: role config and its tests live in steward.","alternativesConsidered":"Store roles in EKA as (now removed) member/assignment artifacts (rejected: re-introduces ownership). Hard-code roles in code only (rejected: inflexible). A single generic worker (rejected: no independent review).","appliesTo":["eka-steward/**"]}